\citation{deerflow2025}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces Overview of the Adaptive Auto-Harness system. \textbf  {Top:} the multi-agent evolver constructs and refines a harness tree across cycles via four phases (Analyze $\to $ Research $\to $ Build $\to $ Verify) with a persistent cross-cycle workspace and temporal-reveal feedback. \textbf  {Bottom:} at solve time, a router agent reads each branch's workspace via \texttt  {git show} and routes the incoming task $x_t$ to the most suitable branch. Two human-in-the-loop hooks (task-board steering and research-phase assistance) trigger only when the evolver's history lacks relevant signal.\relax }}{4}{figure.caption.3}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:unified_pipeline}{{3}{4}{Overview of the Adaptive Auto-Harness system. \textbf {Top:} the multi-agent evolver constructs and refines a harness tree across cycles via four phases (Analyze $\to $ Research $\to $ Build $\to $ Verify) with a persistent cross-cycle workspace and temporal-reveal feedback. \textbf {Bottom:} at solve time, a router agent reads each branch's workspace via \texttt {git show} and routes the incoming task $x_t$ to the most suitable branch. Two human-in-the-loop hooks (task-board steering and research-phase assistance) trigger only when the evolver's history lacks relevant signal.\relax }{figure.caption.3}{}}
